{"title":"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Six squares are drawn and shaded as shown. What fraction of the total area is shaded?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05cc8b5445dc2c01fafa51cd901738d319db18a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> squares are not shaded at all, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> shaded. This means the fraction of the rectangle that is shaded is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/5/9352112e8a302c276438483004bd9640008d73bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times \\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59d1ee70ce5e35ca9c18bc39ad661a503acd439d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312fb7e6460898d86970b3e991b5b145a03e1018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"80\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">1999 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat\">1999 CEM